Z||000000||MR2KLR||12-16-2001||10:06 PM||||<BR>Is there a way I can do it on my 88 Duke? I know you can use a nickle in a 300 tbi what about the 700 TBI?<P>------------------<BR>  <BR>Black 88 Coupe: 120 MPH spedo, Aux. gauge pod, 195/55VR14 Potenza RE-71 tires, GT exhaust & ground F/X Soon to have 16" White Beretta GTZ W/ 215/45ZR16's<BR><A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||12-17-2001||12:25 AM||||before you even consider this you nee a fuel pressure gauge in the input line to the TBI. You should also get an ECM scanner and a FA mix meter with it's own O2 sensor for the exhaust.<P>Get another regulator shell for the 700 and clean out the hole where the screw is. then, acording to some, it's adjustable.... Get another one.... don't screw up the only one you have.<P>Unless you've modded the motor, it's not going to do a thing for you. If you get it too far off the ECM will puke errors. The only time this might do anything is at WOT. Even then unless you know what you are doing you could flood or fry.<P>The 700 TBI used on the Fiero is of the largest made by Delhpi. They are 45mm bore. I think the max Delhpi makes is 48mm.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
